# Source of truth
- PLAN.md is the spec. Read the relevant section before every task. If a request conflicts with PLAN.md, stop and say so. Do not silently pick.
- If something in PLAN.md is ambiguous, ask before coding. State assumptions explicitly.

# Scope
- Build only what the current phase asks. No extra features, settings, or abstractions.
- No backend, no API routes, no auth. All data comes from src/data/*.json.
- Never use the real system clock for data. Use the fixed demo clock from src/lib/time.ts (Tue 6 Oct 2026, 15:00 IST).

# Code
- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Types live in src/types.ts.
- Small components, one job each. No abstraction for single-use code.
- UI copy and guide/annotation text live in src/content, not hardcoded in components.
- Zustand store in src/lib/store.ts. Persist with localStorage wrapped in try/catch.
- Every changed line must trace to the current task. Do not reformat or refactor unrelated code. Mention dead code, do not delete it.

# Design
- Use only the tokens defined in PLAN.md section 8 (CSS variables). No ad hoc hex values in components.
- IBM Plex Sans for UI, IBM Plex Mono only for technical values (IPs, ports, commands, rule names, log values).
- Sentence case. No all-caps labels. No em dashes or en dashes anywhere in UI copy or docs.
- Severity is never color alone: icon + label + color.
- Borders over shadows; shadows only on floating layers.
- Motion only in response to user action. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Every interactive element: keyboard reachable, visible focus ring, aria-label if icon-only.
- Every data view has loading, empty, and error states.
- No Palo Alto Networks logos, trademarks, or brand orange.

# Verification
- After each task: run `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, `npm test`. Fix failures before saying done.
- End every task with: what changed, how you verified it, and anything left open.
